// The `as` row-binder is decoupled from `eff` (G6): on a PURE map it binds a column self-binder `me`
// (`me.col` = this element's bound column, no effect — see each/map_self_binder). Its OTHER use, the
// effectful delete-handle `delete(w)`, is a call/effect, so a pure `map` (transform-only) rejects it —
// the handle form must be written `map (query {…} as w) eff`. Here `delete(w)` in a pure map is rejected.
// RUN: not %arche build -o %t %s 2>&1 | grep -qF "not a column transform"
n :: int;
P :: arche { n }
[8]P ?abort;
bad :: map (query { n } as w) {
  delete(w)(_:);
}
#run seq({ bad })
